Ladybird answers “maybe” for a codec-less type whose container implies
its codec. Gecko and WebKit answer “maybe” for “audio/aac” and
“audio/flac” without a codecs parameter; Blink answers “probably”
(media/base/mime_util_internal.cc treats the implied codec as given).
Gecko’s MP4Decoder::IsSupportedType() accepts “audio/x-m4a” and
“video/quicktime” as MP4, and Blink registers “audio/x-m4a” in
mime_util_internal.cc but not “video/quicktime”; WebKit accepts both
through AVFoundation. Ladybird follows Gecko on both.
